Package: manifest
Title: Document and Report the Impact of the Sampling Framework on the Dataset
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jesse", "Lecy", email = "jdlecy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The manifest package provides a lightweight audit trail for
    data filtering prior to modeling, automating the documentation of
    steps in the workflow that remove observations. It specifically is used in
    the section of the workflow where a researcher applies sample framework criteria
    and discretion to determine which portion of the data is used in models and
    which portion gets dropped. By bracketing the script with `begin_manifest()` and
    `end_manifest()` markers, researchers get a structured log - saved as a timestamped CSV -
    that records for each step: the human-readable rationale (drawn from #: comments
    in the code), the exact code executed, the number and percentage of rows dropped,
    and the rows remaining.
